st play is to **check**, maintaining a low-risk approach with drawing potential. You avoid putting more chips in with a weak pair while preserving the chance to improve on the turn. If a Jack hits, you can reassess (possibly bet or call aggressively). If a blank comes, you can fold or bluff later depending on action. Checking balances risk and reward.\n\nAnswer: 0"}
